<title>USA: US congressman questions Boeing merger plan.</title>
<headline>US congressman questions Boeing merger plan.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-12-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Rep. Bernie Sanders, Independent-Vermont, said Tuesday he feared the proposed merger of Boeing and McDonnell Douglas would reduce competition in the defense and aerospace industries and result in many American workers losing their jobs.</p>
<p>Sanders wrote Defense Secretary William Perry and Attorney General Janet Reno to express his deep concerns about the merger and to ask them to examine it carefully. &quot;I am also writing to demand that no taxpayer dollars be used to subsidize this merger of two multi-billion dollar corporations,&quot; he said.</p>
</text>
